# ADR 044: Keep the game on one page

This record explains why the current game has no router, route state or navigation layer.

## Context

The interface has one continuous activity: choose a board, reveal pairs, inspect status and optionally open reproduction tools. Completion adds a summary to the same board. Importing progress replaces session data. None of those operations requires a separate document location to explain what the user is doing.

The decision is to keep the application as one page with direct component composition and no router. `Game.tsx` renders controls, status, feedback, board and reproduction in a single `main`. The architecture specification explicitly avoids a routing framework for this scope.

## Session transitions are not routes

New Game and Restart replace the game state and increment generation. Loading a board or snapshot validates text and then replaces the state. These transitions have clock and focus consequences, but they do not create URL history entries. The board code is an explicit field and format rather than a path segment.

The reproduction tools use a native `details` disclosure. Opening that panel is a local presentation change, not navigation to a tools screen. The completed banner similarly remains alongside the board and its final statistics. ADR 050 explains why completion keeps that context.

## Why this fits delivery

The artifact opens directly from disk and can also be served from a local origin. Route-based launch would need to account for both path handling and server fallback behavior. A plain code loaded through a control has the same meaning in either context. A copied HTML file does not need a host configured to rewrite route requests.

Browser Back and modifier combinations also retain ordinary browser meanings because the board handles only its stated keys. Introducing a navigation framework would add another consumer of history without a required screen transition to justify it. ADR 003 covers the delivery boundary.

## Alternatives

Separate play, results and reproduction routes might make sense in a larger application with distinct workflows. Here they would force state transfer and focus decisions between screens for information already visible in one small tree. A URL hash for every current selection would also confuse reproducible deal identity with transient progress.

import { useLayoutEffect, useRef } from 'react';
import { Bracket } from './Bracket.tsx';
import { Exchange } from './Exchange.tsx';
import { Setup } from './Setup.tsx';
import { Turn } from './Turn.tsx';
import { decodeTournament, encodeTournament } from './format.ts';
import { matchPlayers, matchStage, matchWinner, TournamentPhase } from './rules.ts';
import type { useTournament } from './use-tournament.ts';
import type { TournamentTurnHandle } from './Turn.tsx';
import './tournament.css';

interface TournamentProps {
  controller: ReturnType<typeof useTournament>;
  back(): void;
  confirm(action: () => void): void;
  publish(text: string): void;
}

export function Tournament({ controller, back, confirm, publish }: TournamentProps) {
  const { state, history } = controller;
  const heading = useRef<HTMLHeadingElement>(null);
  const turn = useRef<TournamentTurnHandle>(null);
  const match = state?.matches[state.currentMatch];
  const phase = state?.phase;
  const completed = phase === TournamentPhase.complete;
  const winner = state && completed ? matchWinner(state, state.currentMatch) : null;
  const player = state
    ? matchPlayers(state, state.currentMatch)[
        phase === TournamentPhase.turnResult ? 0 : (match?.results.length ?? 0) === 0 ? 0 : 1
      ]
    : null;
  const nowPlaying = state && player != null ? `Now playing: ${state.players[player]}` : '';
  const champion = state && winner != null ? `Champion: ${state.players[winner]}` : '';
  useLayoutEffect(() => {
    heading.current?.focus();
    publish(champion || nowPlaying || 'Tournament');
  }, [phase, state?.currentMatch, state?.players]);
  return (
    <section className="tournament">
      <h2 ref={heading} tabIndex={-1}>
        {completed ? 'Tournament complete' : 'Tournament'}
      </h2>
      <p className="help">
        Play the same deal in each match. Fewer moves wins; ties use time, then entry seed.
      </p>
      {!state && <Setup start={controller.start} publish={publish} />}
      {state && (
        <>
          {completed ? (
            <p className="tournament-champion">{champion}</p>
          ) : (
            <>
              <p>Round: {matchStage(state.players.length, state.currentMatch).round}</p>
              <p className="tournament-player">{nowPlaying}</p>
              <div className="tournament-actions">
                {phase === TournamentPhase.ready && (
                  <button className="control" type="button" onClick={controller.startTurn}>
                    Start turn
                  </button>
                )}
                {phase === TournamentPhase.turnResult && (
                  <button className="control" type="button" onClick={controller.advance}>
                    Next turn
                  </button>
                )}
                {phase === TournamentPhase.matchResult && (
                  <button className="control" type="button" onClick={controller.advance}>
                    Next match
                  </button>
                )}
                <button className="control" type="button" onClick={back}>
                  Leave tournament
                </button>
              </div>
            </>
          )}
          {phase === TournamentPhase.playing && state.game && (
            <Turn
              key={`${state.currentMatch}-${match?.results.length}`}
              game={state.game}
              ref={turn}
              update={controller.update}
              publish={publish}
            />
          )}
          {phase === TournamentPhase.matchResult && (
            <p>
              Match winner: {state.players[matchWinner(state, state.currentMatch) ?? 0]} (winner)
            </p>
          )}
          <Bracket state={state} />
        </>
      )}
      {(!state || completed) && (
        <button className="control" type="button" onClick={back}>
          Back to game
        </button>
      )}
      <Exchange
        exportTournament={() => {
          const game = turn.current?.exportGame();
          return encodeTournament(state && game ? { ...state, game } : state);
        }}
        load={(text) => {
          const result = decodeTournament(text);
          if (result.error) {
            publish(result.error);
            return result.error;
          }
          confirm(() => {
            controller.load(result.state ?? null);
            publish('Loaded tournament.');
          });
          return 'Tournament validated.';
        }}
      />
      <section className="past-tournaments" aria-labelledby="past-tournaments-title">
        <h3 id="past-tournaments-title">Past tournaments</h3>
        {history.blocked && <p>Progress won't be saved on this device.</p>}
        {history.items.length === 0 && <p>No finished tournaments yet.</p>}
        <ul>
          {history.items.map((item, index) => (
            <li key={index}>
              <button
                className="control"
                type="button"
                onClick={() => confirm(() => controller.load(item))}
              >
                View tournament {index + 1}: Champion:{' '}
                {item.players[matchWinner(item, item.currentMatch) ?? 0]}
              </button>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </section>
    </section>
  );
}
import { useEffect, useLayoutEffect, useRef } from 'react';
import { isWon } from '../game.ts';
import { SelectionKind } from '../selection.ts';
import { CLOCK_INTERVAL_MS, createClock, elapsedStep } from './browser-clock.ts';
import { tickSession } from './session.ts';
import type { RefObject } from 'react';
import type { Session } from './session.ts';

export function useSessionClock(
  session: Session,
  current: RefObject<Session>,
  commit: (next: Session) => void,
  enabled = true,
) {
  const clock = useRef(createClock(performance.now()));
  const visible = useRef(!document.hidden);
  const won = isWon(session.game);
  const enabledRef = useRef(enabled);

  function running(): boolean {
    return (
      enabledRef.current &&
      visible.current &&
      !current.current.paused &&
      current.current.game.started &&
      !isWon(current.current.game)
    );
  }

  useLayoutEffect(() => {
    synchronize();
    enabledRef.current = enabled;
    clock.current = createClock(performance.now());
  }, [enabled]);

  function synchronize(generation = current.current.generation): void {
    if (generation !== current.current.generation) return;
    const now = performance.now();
    const step = elapsedStep(clock.current, now, running());
    clock.current = step.clock;
    if (step.milliseconds) commit(tickSession(current.current, generation, step.milliseconds));
  }

  useEffect(() => {
    const generation = session.generation;
    let active = true;
    let timer: number | undefined;
    function schedule(): void {
      window.clearTimeout(timer);
      if (!active || generation !== current.current.generation || !running()) return;
      const selection = current.current.game.selection;
      const delay =
        selection.kind === SelectionKind.mismatch
          ? Math.min(CLOCK_INTERVAL_MS, selection.remainingMs)
          : CLOCK_INTERVAL_MS;
      timer = window.setTimeout(() => {
        if (!active) return;
        synchronize(generation);
        schedule();
      }, delay);
    }
    function visibilityChanged(): void {
      if (!active || generation !== current.current.generation) return;
      synchronize(generation);
      visible.current = !document.hidden;
      schedule();
    }
    schedule();
    document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', visibilityChanged);
    return () => {
      active = false;
      window.clearTimeout(timer);
      document.removeEventListener('visibilitychange', visibilityChanged);
    };
  }, [session.generation, session.game.started, session.paused, won, enabled]);

  return {
    synchronize,
    reset: () => {
      clock.current = createClock(performance.now());
    },
  };
}
